1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 Bf5 4. Nf3 e6 5. Be2 c5 6. O-O Qb6?! 7. Be3? { Defends d4 but moves the only guard of b2. Count first: the bishop on c1 guards b2, and nothing else does. The strong reply is 7.c4. } 7... Qxb2 { Black wins a pawn and White's big advantage is gone. } 8. c4 Ne7 *
